# Decky Loader — the plugin host that gives SteamUI features an in-UI surface (Quick Access
# Menu tab). First consumer: the novadeck-control plugin (apps/decky/novadeck-control), the UI for
# /etc/novadeck/game-tweaks.json and the power profiles — settings that until now were
# ssh-edit-a-json-file only.
#
# x86_64 ON PURPOSE. Upstream ships exactly one asset, the x86_64 PyInstaller binary; there is
# no aarch64 build. It runs under the system FEX binfmt (packages/fex-emu) — the same mechanism
# as native x86 Linux games, a combination already proven on aarch64 handhelds elsewhere, with
# the AppConfig knobs we mirror in rootfs/overlay/usr/share/fex-emu/AppConfig/PluginLoader.json
# (TSO on, Multiblock off, GL/Vulkan/Wayland/asound thunks). A Python runtime is far tamer
# under emulation than a game: no JIT of its own, no GPU fast path to lose.
#
# THE BINARY IS THE STABLE BUILD; NEW INSTALLS STILL TRACK PRERELEASE. Those are two separate
# things and they are set in two places.
#
# This pin was on v3.2.8-pre1 because the -pre channel is where upstream lands its Steam-on-ARM
# fixes (native arm64 Steam client, which is what this image runs) while the stable channel targets
# the x86 Deck client. v3.2.8 is that same version promoted to stable on 2026-09-02, so it carries
# those fixes and is strictly newer than the -pre1 we were on: taking it costs nothing and gains
# whatever landed between the two.
#
# The seeded loader.json (written by /usr/lib/novadeck/decky-sync, {"branch": 1}) is UNCHANGED and
# still points new installs at the prerelease branch, for the original reason — the next fix we need
# will land there first, and Decky self-updates from that channel. Shipping a stable binary and
# tracking prerelease is not a contradiction: the pin decides what the image contains, the branch
# decides what the loader upgrades itself to.
#
# mode: PluginLoader is executed directly by plugin_loader.service; without 0755 the unit fails
# with EACCES (kind:file installs 0644 by default — right for the FEX rootfs image, not for a
# binary).
#
# Fields: see packages/inputplumber/prebuilt.pin for the base set and
# packages/fex-rootfs/prebuilt.pin for kind/dest; this pin adds
#   mode -> chmod for the placed file (kind:file only; default 0644)
#
# To bump: pick a release at https://github.com/SteamDeckHomebrew/decky-loader/releases, set
# version + url together, and recompute sha256 from the downloaded asset (upstream publishes no
# checksum sidecar).
name: decky-loader
version: v3.2.8
url: https://github.com/SteamDeckHomebrew/decky-loader/releases/download/v3.2.8/PluginLoader
sha256: 4b9a04a1ac4ed0c028dcbbc38cd03383eb438d69744d613775c93f81809afde2
kind: file
dest: /usr/share/decky-loader/PluginLoader
mode: 0755
